**No data is required to browse or download the datasets.**

We only collect data if you create an account:

- your **email address**;
- if you choose “Continue with Google”: your Google **name** and **profile picture**;
- the **optional** information you add to your profile: username, display name, bio, website and avatar.

When you sign up, a username is created automatically from the beginning of your email address. It is public: you can change it at any time in [My profile](/profile).

The website relies on these services:

- **Supabase**: accounts and database;
- **Cloudflare**: storage and delivery of data files;
- **Vercel**: website hosting and anonymous visit statistics (Vercel Analytics, without cookies);
- **OpenStreetMap**: base map of the globes shown on dataset pages;
- **Google**: only if you choose “Continue with Google”.

As with any website, these services receive technical information (IP address, browser type) needed to display pages and serve files. Some of them may process it outside the European Union.

Under the GDPR, you can at any time:

- **access** your data;
- **correct** it, directly from [My profile](/profile);
- ask for the **deletion** of your account and data, simply by writing to [newalgeria.org@gmail.com](mailto:newalgeria.org@gmail.com).

We reply within one month at most. If you believe your rights are not respected, you can contact the French data protection authority, the [CNIL](https://www.cnil.fr).

You are responsible for your account and the information in your profile. Keep your password to yourself.

- one account per person;
- no impersonation.
